  "verdict": "SAMPLERS_INDISTINGUISHABLE",
  "honest_framing": "MEASURED only. A negative verdict (SAMPLERS_INDISTINGUISHABLE) licenses the abstract's sentence; a positive one means the sentence must be reworded. The test is two-sided because the hypothesis under test is 'no difference', and it is Holm-corrected within the 6-pair family. Pooled means are reported but Ru is ~64% of the cohort, so per-metal means are the load-bearing view. PAIRING CAVEAT: the sampler draws the K support rows and the query is held-out-minus-support, so the four arms do NOT share a query set — n_query is identical but the zero-shot AUC is not. The contrast is therefore reported twice, on the absolute adapted AUC and on the delta-vs-zero-shot, and the verdict requires both to be indistinguishable. This is the same (metal, seed) cell structure the published C3 family uses (n_cells=25), so the test is consistent with it."
